<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gaius Sextius Calvinus</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">fl. 124–122 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/2nd-century-bce">2nd century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Gaius Sextius Calvinus was a Roman consul of 124 BCE who campaigned against the Salyes of southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gaul">Gaul</a> at the request of Massalia. He completed the destruction of their stronghold of Entremont and in 122 BCE founded the garrison settlement of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aix-en-provence">Aquae Sextiae</a>, modern Aix-en-Provence, named after himself and its hot springs. He celebrated a triumph over the Ligurians, Vocontii and Salluvii.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/gaius-sextius-calvinus.jpg" alt="Gaius Sextius Calvinus" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Malost · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Caius_Sextius_Calvinus.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
